[{"category":"section","location":"#GaussManinResurgence","page":"Home","text":"Documentation for GaussManinResurgence.\n\n","title":"GaussManinResurgence"},{"category":"type","location":"#GaussManinResurgence.Expansion","page":"Home","text":"Expansion consists of a f₀ and Tₘ\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GaussManinResurgence.Expansion"},{"category":"method","location":"#GaussManinResurgence.BorelPadeResum-Tuple{Any, Any}","page":"Home","text":"Resumation with Borel-Pade\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GaussManinResurgence.BorelPadeResum"},{"category":"method","location":"#GaussManinResurgence.BorelTransform-Tuple{Any, Any}","page":"Home","text":"Borel transform: Σₘ Tₘ / kᵐ ↦ Σₘ Tₘ / Γ(m + α) tᵐ\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GaussManinResurgence.BorelTransform"},{"category":"method","location":"#GaussManinResurgence.GaussManin-Tuple{Any}","page":"Home","text":"Build the Gauss-Manin system.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GaussManinResurgence.GaussManin"},{"category":"method","location":"#GaussManinResurgence.PadeEvaluate-Tuple{Any, Any, Any}","page":"Home","text":"pade_eval(num, den, x)\n\nEvaluate the rational approximant.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GaussManinResurgence.PadeEvaluate"},{"category":"method","location":"#GaussManinResurgence.TaylorToPade-Tuple{AbstractVector, Int64, Int64}","page":"Home","text":"TaylorToPade(a, m, n)\n\nCompute the [m/n] Padé approximant from Taylor coefficients a, where a[k+1] is the coefficient of x^k.\n\nReturns (num, den) where\n\nnum are numerator coefficients in increasing order\nden are denominator coefficients in increasing order, with den[1] == 1\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GaussManinResurgence.TaylorToPade"},{"category":"method","location":"#GaussManinResurgence.asymptotic-Tuple{Any, GaussManinSystem, Any}","page":"Home","text":"Evaluate the asymptotic series expansion.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GaussManinResurgence.asymptotic"},{"category":"method","location":"#GaussManinResurgence.base_value-Tuple{Any, Any, Any}","page":"Home","text":"L(z0) on the principal branch: straight path from the (tangential) base point 0.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GaussManinResurgence.base_value"},{"category":"method","location":"#GaussManinResurgence.continue_along-NTuple{4, Any}","page":"Home","text":"L^γ(z0) for a sequence of loops, e.g. [(2,+1),(3,-1)] = around σ2 ccw, then σ3 cw.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GaussManinResurgence.continue_along"},{"category":"function","location":"#GaussManinResurgence.evaluateAdjacency","page":"Home","text":"Evaluate the adjacency without Stokes constants\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GaussManinResurgence.evaluateAdjacency"},{"category":"method","location":"#GaussManinResurgence.evaluate_series_by_weight-Tuple{Dict{Vector{Int64}, ComplexF64}, Any, Any}","page":"Home","text":"Weight-resolved evaluation: D[r+1] is the contribution of the words of length r.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GaussManinResurgence.evaluate_series_by_weight"},{"category":"method","location":"#GaussManinResurgence.findAllSaddles-Tuple{DynamicPolynomials.Polynomial}","page":"Home","text":"Find all saddles of a multivariate polynomial\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GaussManinResurgence.findAllSaddles"},{"category":"method","location":"#GaussManinResurgence.findPoles-Tuple{Any}","page":"Home","text":"Find poles\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GaussManinResurgence.findPoles"},{"category":"function","location":"#GaussManinResurgence.findStokesConstants","page":"Home","text":"Find the Stokes constants\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GaussManinResurgence.findStokesConstants"},{"category":"method","location":"#GaussManinResurgence.local_singular-NTuple{4, Any}","page":"Home","text":"Local solution at the singular point σj:  Lj(z) = H(z-σj) exp(xj log(z-σj)), H holomorphic with H(0) = 1 (principal branch of log). Needs |z-σj| < dist to other letters. Solves  k hk - [xj, hk] = Σm Am h{k-1-m}  order by order.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GaussManinResurgence.local_singular"},{"category":"method","location":"#GaussManinResurgence.loop_path-Tuple{Any, Any, Any}","page":"Home","text":"Polyline for the loop: z0 → straight to radius r around σ_i → circle (ccw if orient=+1) → back.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GaussManinResurgence.loop_path"},{"category":"method","location":"#GaussManinResurgence.monodromy_factor-NTuple{4, Any}","page":"Home","text":"Monodromy factor M with L^γ(z0) = L(z0) · M for the loop around σi based at z0 (straight segment z0 → σi, one turn, back). Returns (M, C), C the regularised value at σ_i.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GaussManinResurgence.monodromy_factor"},{"category":"method","location":"#GaussManinResurgence.monodromy_pieces-NTuple{4, Any}","page":"Home","text":"Based monodromy matrices T[j] of  Y' = Σs Rs/(z-σs) Y  for the ccw loops around σj (base point z0, straight stems), weight-resolved: T[j][r+1] is the weight-r part.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GaussManinResurgence.monodromy_pieces"},{"category":"method","location":"#GaussManinResurgence.mul-Tuple{Dict{Vector{Int64}, ComplexF64}, Dict{Vector{Int64}, ComplexF64}, Int64}","page":"Home","text":"Concatenation product, truncated at weight N.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GaussManinResurgence.mul"},{"category":"method","location":"#GaussManinResurgence.plotA-Tuple{Any, Any}","page":"Home","text":"Plot the evaluated coefficients A.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GaussManinResurgence.plotA"},{"category":"function","location":"#GaussManinResurgence.plotAdjacency","page":"Home","text":"Plot the evaluated coefficients A.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GaussManinResurgence.plotAdjacency"},{"category":"function","location":"#GaussManinResurgence.plotAdjacencyPoles","page":"Home","text":"Plot the evaluated coefficients A.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GaussManinResurgence.plotAdjacencyPoles"},{"category":"method","location":"#GaussManinResurgence.polyEvaluate-Tuple{Any, Any}","page":"Home","text":"poly_eval(c, x)\n\nEvaluate polynomial with coefficients in increasing order.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GaussManinResurgence.polyEvaluate"},{"category":"function","location":"#GaussManinResurgence.refineSaddle","page":"Home","text":"Refine saddle\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GaussManinResurgence.refineSaddle"},{"category":"method","location":"#GaussManinResurgence.regular_transport-NTuple{4, Any}","page":"Home","text":"Transport series Ga(b) = Σw L^{(a)}_w(b) w with base point a (a regular point), by Taylor expansion in u = t-a. Needs |b-a| < dist(a, Σ).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GaussManinResurgence.regular_transport"},{"category":"method","location":"#GaussManinResurgence.sexp-Tuple{Dict{Vector{Int64}, ComplexF64}, Any}","page":"Home","text":"exp(A) for A without constant term.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GaussManinResurgence.sexp"},{"category":"method","location":"#GaussManinResurgence.sinv-Tuple{Dict{Vector{Int64}, ComplexF64}, Any}","page":"Home","text":"Inverse of a series with invertible constant term.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GaussManinResurgence.sinv"},{"category":"method","location":"#GaussManinResurgence.transport-NTuple{4, Any}","page":"Home","text":"Continue a solution L (given at path[1]) along the polyline path, left-multiplying transports.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GaussManinResurgence.transport"}]
